  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $15.98B (+0.6% 30D) keeps on-chain RWA exposure in a holding pattern\u2014tokenization momentum is still news- and pipeline-driven until distributed value breaks range. Related: <a href=\"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiywFBVV95cUxOTUN3RTRsbnMxclFCNERCcE5JSF90aFBFMFNOWUN6eGpBRFJxb3EybXBnNWdvdHgyRE53dVlMNWctUTFSbjFBcllZb3REaVUzeEZRZGFieFVQNmItaDc1T0RadlhGdTFIN1M0djVQQUtBX3dwTFVLb0p0YkdfUndCd2IybXBJSFF1OU9UVDF5dlJIa1VVUmYwM2RKdmlhRTVCTWJGTGw0cVJDRlIyRlYxc0FlU0IydG9UbmFna3FUV0VOSVpINmFhUi1xQQ?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Injective becomes SEC-registered transfer agent as it expands tokenization push</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows.</li><li><strong>Tokenized T-bill supply is still expanding through new products:</strong> That usually shows up first as new issuer and product supply, then as higher distributed value and denser collateral-style use across networks and platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/opinion/2026/08/21/the-hard-truth-is-that-the-clarity-act-is-an-anti-crypto-bill\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The hard truth is that the Clarity Act is an anti-crypto bill</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/08/21/nomura-backed-laser-digital-wins-japan-s-first-crypto-approval-in-four-years\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nomura-backed Laser Digital wins Japan&#x27;s first crypto approval in four years</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
